  <entry>
    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2607.24999v2</id>
    <title>CogBattery: Human-Referenced Evaluation of Cognitive Task Behavior and Structure in Language Models</title>
    <updated>2026-10-30T13:55:34Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.24999v2" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2607.24999v2" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>Human cognitive tasks let us compare language models with humans under controlled conditions. Yet a model can reproduce the direction of a human effect while making different errors. CogBattery evaluates 54 open-weight language models on text adaptations of 13 cognitive paradigms, comparing each with human data from its source study. Like humans, models respond more to n-back lures than to controls, yet they make far more false alarms on ordinary non-targets. Most models' reported confidence separates correct from incorrect answers less well than humans' does, and most always choose the same wager, including models that classify accurately. These patterns span many model families. Across tasks, model scores share two dimensions. The first is closely tied to scale, yet larger models are not consistently closer to humans. Predefined cognitive groupings show no reliable predictive advantage over random groupings of the same size. These results show that matching human effect directions does not establish human-like behavior. CogBattery provides condition-level human references for testing errors and confidence reports in new models.</summary>
    <category term="cs.CL" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <category term="cs.AI" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <category term="q-bio.NC" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <published>2026-07-27T18:56:13Z</published>
    <arxiv:comment>13 pages, 3 figures, 5 tables. Code at https://github.com/dengzhe-hou/CogBattery. Renamed from CogArena to avoid confusion with an unrelated benchmark of the same name</arxiv:comment>
    <arxiv:primary_category term="cs.CL"/>
    <author>
      <name>Dengzhe Hou</name>
    </author>
    <author>
      <name>Lingyu Jiang</name>
    </author>
    <author>
      <name>Fangzhou Lin</name>
    </author>
    <author>
      <name>Kazunori D Yamada</name>
    </author>
