  <entry>
    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2501.08686v2</id>
    <title>Knowledge Graph-based Retrieval-Augmented Generation for Schema Matching</title>
    <updated>2026-11-06T14:56:30Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.08686v2" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2501.08686v2" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>Traditional similarity-based schema matching methods fail to resolve semantic ambiguities and conflicts in complex, domain-specific mappings due to a lack of commonsense and domain-specific knowledge. In parallel, large language models (LLMs) without sufficient background knowledge tend to hallucinate, further complicating schema matching. To overcome these limitations, we introduce KG-RAG4SM, a Knowledge Graph-based Retrieval-Augmented Generation for Schema Matching. This method integrates novel retrieval mechanisms, including LLM-based, vector-based, graph traversal-based, and hybrid techniques with advanced reranking schemes to extract the most relevant subgraphs from large external KGs. Our approach achieves superior results without requiring re-training, as evidenced by improvements of 39.79% in precision and 30.56% in F1 score over LLM-based state-of-the-art (SOTA) methods (e.g., Jellyfish-8B) on the MIMIC dataset, and enhancements of 69.20% in precision and 21.99% in F1 score over pre-trained language model (PLM)-based SOTA methods (e.g., SMAT) on the Synthea dataset. Additionally, KG-RAG4SM scales effectively across KGs from commonsense KGs to domain-specific ones, while its instruction-tuning knowledge exclusion component ensures truthful performance in end-to-end schema matching tasks despite the suboptimal relevance of KG context. Our empirical analysis and case studies from real-world scenarios show that the hallucination problem in LLMs for schema matching is well mitigated by our solution.</summary>
    <category term="cs.DB" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <category term="cs.CL" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <category term="cs.IR" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <published>2025-01-15T09:32:37Z</published>
    <arxiv:comment>To appear in ACM TKDD</arxiv:comment>
    <arxiv:primary_category term="cs.DB"/>
    <author>
      <name>Chuangtao Ma</name>
    </author>
    <author>
      <name>Sriom Chakrabarti</name>
    </author>
    <author>
      <name>Arijit Khan</name>
    </author>
    <author>
      <name>Bálint Molnár</name>
    </author>
    <arxiv:doi>10.1145/3862591</arxiv:doi>
